  <prompt>Any signed-in caller can list, read, create, edit, complete, cancel and soft-delete any sprk_event in the tenant through /api/v1/events, because every route checks only sign-in and then reads or writes through the BFF's app-only Dataverse client on an id the caller chooses. Make each of the eight routes ask Dataverse, as the caller, about the exact record the handler touches, before any Dataverse read or write, and fail closed. Trim the list to what the caller can read. Separately, repair how this API writes and reads the event's regarding record: sprk_regardingrecordtype is a lookup to sprk_recordtype_ref, and today the create payload, the update payload, the list filter, the $select and the mapper all treat it as an integer.</prompt>

  <amendments source="main session, 2026-10-03, owner rounds 9-10" binding="true">
    <!-- Read these before step 0. Each overrides anything below that contradicts it. -->
    <amendment>Owner decisions now run to round 10: re-read notes/session27-owner-decisions-and-research.md rounds 9 and 10 on work/unified-access-control-r2 before step 0. They are newer than this POML.</amendment>
    <amendment>Do NOT rename or move FinanceAuthorizationFilter, and do not create a RecordAccessAuthorizationFilter or any other generalized copy of it: reuse it as it is. The rename is follow-up task 170, after the sweep tasks are integrated. Several sweep tasks reuse this filter in parallel, and a move in one of them would conflict with all the others.</amendment>
    <amendment>Task 167 (the every-route guard) runs IN PARALLEL with this task. If RouteAuthorizationGuardTests on your branch has no Pending waiver for your routes (167 not yet landed), do NOT add waivers, ledger entries or Permanent waivers, and do NOT add your files to GovernedFiles. Instead, add a table "Route authorization ledger input" to your task note, with one row per route you changed or deleted: the route key exactly as the guard spells it (VERB /path), the mechanism that now decides (filter, probe or impersonation), the deny test (its fully qualified name, proving a caller without rights is refused), and, for a list whose query runs AS the caller, the words "handler decision: query runs as the caller". The main session records these in 167's ledger at integration. If 167 HAS landed on your branch, follow its ledger contract: delete your Pending waivers and set ResolvedBy and ProofTest in the same diff.</amendment>
    <amendment>Owner round 10 item 1 (BINDING): delete a route when it has NO caller in the repo AND it is NOT in any published API description; fix it otherwise. Search the repo for OpenAPI documents and Copilot or agent plugin manifests (for example *openapi*, ai-plugin*, *manifest*.json, declarativeAgent*) before you decide. List every deletion, with its no-caller and not-published evidence, in the note and the PR. Delete the services, filters and options that only the deleted routes used. Keep the file census count in RouteAuthorizationGuardTests right if a whole endpoint file goes.</amendment>
    <amendment>Impersonation: never assign ServiceClient.CallerId or CallerAADObjectId outside Spaarke.Dataverse/DataverseImpersonation.cs (task 160 adds the single SDK entry point there, plus an arch rule). For the Web API, impersonate through DataverseWebApiService's existing impersonateSystemUserId parameter (MSCRMCallerID). It refuses Guid.Empty (task 104).</amendment>
    <amendment>Soft delete (DELETE /{id}, and a PUT that sets the Deleted status) requires WRITE on the event, not the Delete privilege. It is a status update, and Dataverse's own answer for the operation performed decides (owner D1). This overrides the Delete requirement written below.</amendment>
    <amendment>Event status values: read the live statuscode options in step 0. If EventDto's 1-7 values do not match live (TaskActionCore and DailyBriefingCollector use 659490001 and up), fix the mapping in this task so complete, cancel and delete work against the live values, and include TodoGenerationService's status filter. It is a defect on the same routes, not an owner question.</amendment>
    <amendment>GET /api/v1/events is a "query runs as the caller" handler decision for task 167's ledger, NOT a Permanent waiver. Do not add a Permanent waiver for it.</amendment>
  </amendments>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer: BFF authorization endpoint filters (ADR-008), the caller-scoped Dataverse access seam (CallerRecordAccessProbe over OBO, MSCRMCallerID impersonation through DataverseImpersonation), ProblemDetails (ADR-019), the ADR-024 polymorphic regarding pattern and the FR-26 core-ancestor stamp (CoreAncestorResolver). Fail closed (ADR-003).</role>

  <goal>After this task:
(1) GET /api/v1/events runs its query AS the caller (MSCRMCallerID impersonation with the caller's systemuserid), so every row, the TotalCount and every page are only what the caller may read. A caller who does not resolve to a systemuser gets 403 and no query runs. regardingRecordId must be a GUID (anything else is a 400 and no query runs), so no caller text reaches $filter.
(2) GET /{id}, GET /{id}/logs, PUT /{id}, DELETE /{id}, POST /{id}/complete and POST /{id}/cancel each carry an endpoint filter that asks Dataverse (RetrievePrincipalAccess over the caller's OBO token) for the caller's rights on sprk_events({id}) before the handler runs. A caller without Read on the event, and a caller naming an id that does not exist, get the IDENTICAL 404. A caller who holds Read but not the required right gets 403.
(3) POST /api/v1/events checks, as the caller, the Create privilege on sprk_event and, when a regarding record is given, AppendTo on it, before any Dataverse write. An unknown regarding id and a denied one get the identical 403.
(4) PUT /{id} whose body carries RegardingRecordType/RegardingRecordId also checks Write and Append on the event and AppendTo on the NEW regarding record. PUT whose body sets StatusCode to EventStatusCode.Deleted also checks Delete, the same right DELETE /{id} requires.
(5) The create and update payloads write the ADR-024 regarding set in the correct Web API shape: the target's own typed lookup bound by its live navigation-property name and live entity-set name; sprk_regardingrecordtype bound to its sprk_recordtype_ref row; the denormalized id, name and url (and number where the column exists); then the FR-26 core-ancestor stamps. On a re-parent, every other sprk_regarding* lookup is cleared in the same PATCH. The read side (list filter, $select, mapper) reads the lookup as a lookup.
(6) EventEndpoints.cs is governed by RouteAuthorizationGuardTests (Scope.RouteLevelGate). The seven id/create routes pass Rule A with a real filter. The list carries one Permanent "query-is-the-gate" waiver in the word-add-in-r1 task 062 form. Every Pending waiver task 167 added for these eight routes is deleted or replaced as constraint "waivers" says.
(7) The behaviour is proven live in dev by the main session with existing non-admin test users.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>🔴 LIVE. Every anchor below was verified on 2026-10-02 against work/unified-access-control-r2 @ b18a7d321. Line numbers drift by a few lines between branches; re-verify each in step 0.

THE GROUP. `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Events/EventEndpoints.cs:32-35` maps `/api/v1/events` with `.RequireRateLimiting("dataverse-query")` and a bare `.RequireAuthorization()`. The BFF has no DefaultPolicy or FallbackPolicy override, so that means "signed in". No route in the file has an endpoint filter. The group is mapped unconditionally at `Infrastructure/DI/EndpointMappingExtensions.cs:239`. `IEventDataverseService` resolves to the singleton `DataverseWebApiService` (`Infrastructure/DI/GraphModule.cs:100`), which authenticates as the BFF's own identity. `CreateAuthenticatedRequestAsync` (`src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/DataverseWebApiService.cs:199-218`) sends MSCRMCallerID ONLY when `impersonateSystemUserId` is passed (and refuses Guid.Empty, task 104); no event method passes it. Every event read and write is therefore app-only, and Dataverse row security never applies to the caller.

THE EIGHT ROUTES (evidence file idor-group-159.json; sweep rows 11-16, 37, 38):
  • GET / (`:38`, handler `GetEventsAsync` `:146-268`). Owner narrowing `_ownerid_value eq caller` is added only when the oid resolves to a systemuser (`:218-228`, via `ICommunicationDataverseService.QuerySystemUserByAzureAdOidAsync`). An unresolvable caller gets every event in the tenant. `regardingRecordId` is a string concatenated unescaped into `$filter` (`DataverseWebApiService.cs:330-331`) and the filters are joined with " and " (`:348`), so a value such as `x' or sprk_regardingrecordid ne 'zz` bypasses the owner clause ("and" binds tighter than "or"). CRITICAL.
  • GET /{id} (`:48`, `GetEventByIdAsync` `:278-320`). No caller parameter at all. Returns description and every regarding lookup (`DataverseWebApiService.cs:375-407`); 404-vs-200 is an existence oracle. CRITICAL.
  • DELETE /{id} (`:58`, `DeleteEventAsync` `:555-595` → `SoftDeleteEventAsync` `:702-716`). Sets statuscode Deleted (7) and writes an event-log row, app-only. (The route's own description at `:57-62` says "Canceled"; the code sets Deleted.) CRITICAL.
  • POST / (`:69`, `CreateEventAsync` `:335-436` → `CreateEventInDataverseAsync` `:765-797` → `DataverseWebApiService.CreateEventAsync` `:409-430`). Only shape validation; the caller-chosen RegardingRecordType/RegardingRecordId are bound app-only. `ResolveActingUserContactAsync` (`:722-757`, task 152) fills sprk_assignedto and authorizes nothing. HIGH.
  • PUT /{id} (`:80`, `UpdateEventAsync` `:446-545` → `UpdateEventInDataverseAsync` `:805-838`). Overwrites every field, including StatusCode 1-7 and the regarding triple, so any user can re-parent any event into or out of a secure matter. CRITICAL.
  • POST /{id}/complete (`:92`, `CompleteEventAsync` `:883-958`) and POST /{id}/cancel (`:105`, `CancelEventAsync` `:968-1043`). Existence read, status-transition check (`CanCompleteEvent`/`CanCancelEvent` `:1060-1085`), app-only status PATCH (`DataverseWebApiService.cs:530-552`, no impersonation at `:548`), event-log row. CRITICAL.
  • GET /{id}/logs (`:118`, `GetEventLogsAsync` `:1133-1180` → `QueryEventLogsAsync` `DataverseWebApiService.cs:554-580`). Returns every log row's action, notes and createdby name. HIGH.
RouteAuthorizationGuardTests has no entry for EventEndpoints.cs on this branch (it is NotGoverned by omission).

THE REGARDING SHAPE DEFECT (#1098 second half — wider than #1098 says). `sprk_event.sprk_regardingrecordtype` is a LOOKUP to `sprk_recordtype_ref` (`docs/data-model/sprk_event-related-tables.md:104`; `.claude/adr/ADR-024-polymorphic-resolver-pattern.md` "Resolver Fields" and MUST rules `:76-93`). This API treats it as an integer option set (`Api/Events/Dtos/EventDto.cs:166-169`, comment "matches sprk_regardingrecordtype option set") in FIVE places:
  (a) UPDATE — `DataverseWebApiService.UpdateEventAsync` `:509-514` writes `sprk_regardingrecordtype` = an integer plus id/name, and never writes or clears any typed regarding lookup. A re-parent would leave the typed lookup on the OLD record (ADR-024 `:79`/`:81`: one typed lookup; clear the previous one).
  (b) CREATE — `BuildCreateEventPayload` `:437-480` writes the same integer at `:467`, and binds the typed lookup with the LOGICAL name as the navigation property and a PLURALIZED set name, `/{entityName}s({id})` at `:476` (wrong for sprk_analysis, whose set is not "sprk_analysiss"; navigation-property casing on sprk_event is not verified anywhere). So the create path is NOT a correct reference shape.
  (c) LIST FILTER — `QueryEventsAsync` `:327-328` filters `sprk_regardingrecordtype eq an integer`.
  (d) $SELECT — `:349` (list) and `:378` (get) select `sprk_regardingrecordtype` by its logical name.
  (e) MAPPING — `MapToEventEntity` `:1685-1745` reads `sprk_regardingrecordtype` with `GetInt32()` (`:1723-1724`); the list's $select carries none of the typed `_sprk_regarding*_value` columns.
If the docs are right, (d) means GET / and GET /{id} may be failing live today (the Web API exposes a lookup as `_x_value`, and a $select of the logical name is rejected), and (a)/(b) reject any request that carries a regarding type. Step 0 settles this read-only.
The CORRECT shape comes from the ADR-024 builders, not from this API's create path:
  • `Services/Workspace/TodoRegardingBuilder.cs:131-280` (`ApplyResolverFieldsAsync`): one typed lookup for the target; `sprk_regardingrecordtype` as a reference to the `sprk_recordtype_ref` row found by `ICommunicationDataverseService.QueryRecordTypeRefAsync(entityLogicalName)` (`:238-265`), non-fatal when absent (log, leave unset); `sprk_regardingrecordid` = lowercase "D" GUID; `sprk_regardingrecordname`; `sprk_regardingrecordurl` = `TodoRegardingBuilder.BuildRecordUrl` (`:276-279`, relative main.aspx URL); then the FR-26 core-ancestor stamp LAST, failing closed (`:202-222`).
  • The Web API flavour of the same set: `Services/Finance/InvoiceReviewService.cs:284-300` — lookups written ONLY as `{navigationProperty}@odata.bind`, never as `_x_value` keys; `InvRegardingRecordTypeBind = "sprk_regardingrecordtype@odata.bind"` (`:293`, the navigation-property name read from live metadata for sprk_invoice); the record-type row resolved per environment (`ResolveMatterRecordTypeIdAsync` `:694-716`).
  • Name/number resolution precedent: `src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/DataverseServiceClientImpl.cs:500-542` with `RegardingRecordType.GetPrimaryNameField` / `GetReferenceNumberField` (`Models.cs:1262-1276`, matter and project only).
  • THE CORE-ANCESTOR STAMP ON A WEB API BODY. `Services/Dataverse/CoreAncestorResolver.cs`: `StampAsync` (`:400`, `:424`) writes SDK `EntityReference` values into an `Entity` or a `Dictionary`, which is NOT a Web API JSON body. For a hand-written JSON body the resolver provides `DeriveForHostAsync(hostEntityLogicalName, targetEntityLogicalName, targetRecordId, ct)` (`:452`): it returns the stamps without applying them, and the caller emits each one in its own payload shape under the same fail-closed contract. sprk_event is a CHILD entity (`:74-82`) and carries all four core stamp columns (`:91-95`): `sprk_regardingproject`, `sprk_regardingmatter`, `sprk_regardingworkassignment`, `sprk_regardingservicerequest` (`:97-103`). These are the SAME columns as the typed regarding lookups for project, matter and work assignment. So an event regarding an invoice or an analysis carries TWO lookups after a correct write: its own typed lookup and the stamp of its core ancestor (the TodoRegardingBuilder precedent, `:202-206`). "Exactly one typed lookup" is therefore wrong as a rule for this task; the rule is in constraint "regarding write shape". `CoreAncestorResolver` is registered unconditionally (`Program.cs:81` → `AddDataverseMetadataServices` → `MetadataServiceExtensions.cs:31`).
  • `Services/Ai/Nodes/ActionCore/TaskActionCore.cs:85-105` is sprk_event's own typed-lookup family (14 targets, including sprk_regardingorganization, sprk_regardingcommunication, sprk_regardingevent, sprk_regardingreportcard and sprk_regardingservicerequest, none of which the API's 0-7 types use); its core stamp is at `:160-185`.
  • LAYERING. `BuildCreateEventPayload` lives in `Spaarke.Dataverse`, which cannot reference `Sprk.Bff.Api` (CoreAncestorResolver, TodoRegardingBuilder) and whose `DataverseWebApiService` does not implement `ICommunicationDataverseService`. So the record-type row, the server-resolved name, the entity set and the core stamps are resolved in the BFF (the handler) and passed into the Dataverse request model as plain values; the static builder only shapes them.

A SECOND MISMATCH, NOT AUTHORIZATION (escalation trigger 2). `Api/Events/Dtos/EventDto.cs:117-141` uses statuscode Draft 1 / Planned 2 / Open 3 / OnHold 4 / Completed 5 / Cancelled 6 / Deleted 7, and `BuildCreateEventPayload` writes statuscode 3 (`:443`). Two comments that say they were checked against the live option set give different values: `Services/Ai/Nodes/ActionCore/TaskActionCore.cs:62-68` ("Draft(1) / Open(659490001) / Completed(659490002) / Cancelled(659490004)") and `Services/Ai/Narrators/DailyBriefingCollector.cs:128` (`EventStatusOpen = 659490001`). If live agrees with those, complete, cancel, delete, PUT StatusCode, the list's status alias (`EventEndpoints.cs:177-189`) and `TodoGenerationService.cs:409`/`:577` all write or filter values that do not exist, so the live gate's positive cases on those routes cannot pass.

CLIENTS. The only shipped consumer in src is the Copilot agent plugin, `src/solutions/CopilotAgent/spaarke-bff-openapi.yaml:440-552` (listEvents "for the authenticated user", createEvent, getEvent, completeEvent), which calls the BFF with the user's delegated token. It types `regardingRecordId` as a string described "ID of the related record"; after this task a non-GUID value is a 400 where it used to return an empty list. No PCF, code page or web resource calls /api/v1/events (grep of src for "v1/events": the OpenAPI file, the endpoint file and its DTOs only). Two background callers use the app-only query and must stay app-only: `Services/Workspace/TodoGenerationService.cs:403` and `:570`.

REUSE, NOT NEW MACHINERY (read each before choosing):
  • `Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/CallerRecordAccessProbe.cs` — `GetCallerRightsAsync(token, entitySet, recordId)` (`:212-244`, virtual): OBO, WhoAmI, RetrievePrincipalAccess, uncached, `AccessRights.None` on every fault. Under OBO, Dataverse answers "not found" both for a missing record and for one the caller cannot see, so the two are indistinguishable by construction (with a ~1.6 s retry on not-found, `:101-106`). `CallerHoldsPrivilegeAsync(token, privilegeName)` (`:386-452`, virtual): the caller's table privilege, uncached, false on every fault. READ-ONLY for this task (constraint "ExternalAccess zones").
  • `Api/Filters/RecordRouteAccessAuthorizationFilter.cs:24-37` (extension `AddRecordRouteAccessAuthorizationFilter(operation)`) and `:79-232` (filter): the existing route-value → CallerRecordAccessProbe → `OperationAccessPolicy.HasRequiredRights` → fail-closed endpoint filter (task 076, attached at `Api/OBOEndpoints.cs`). Its route keys are FIXED to `{entityLogicalName}`/`{recordId}` (`:105`, `:108`), its entity set comes from `EntityAccessFilter.TryResolveEntitySet`, every denial is a 403 via `ProblemDetailsHelper.Forbidden` with SHORT reasonCodes (`owning_record_not_specified`, `entity_type_not_authorizable`, `access_check_failed`, `insufficient_rights`), and its deny detail reads "You do not have permission to add content to this record." So it does not fit these routes as-is. Task 130's justification named it "the first candidate to EXTEND (route key, fixed entity type, deny status)"; task 130 itself extended FinanceAuthorizationFilter instead, so the parameterization has not been done yet.
  • `Api/Filters/FinanceAuthorizationFilter.cs:280-290` — `UniformRecordNotFound(httpContext)`, the byte-stable uniform 404 (title "Not Found", detail "The requested record was not found.", reasonCode `sdap.access.deny.record_unavailable` `:256`, extension `correlationId`), pinned by task 130's contract tests (`FinanceEndpointsAuthorizationContractTests.cs:137`). `:237` — `CreateInvoicePrivilege = "prvCreatesprk_Invoice"`, the live-verified privilege-name constant precedent. `:240`/`:246` — `InsufficientRightsReasonCode = "sdap.access.deny.insufficient_rights"` and `InsufficientPrivilegeReasonCode = "sdap.access.deny.insufficient_privilege"`.
  • `Infrastructure/Errors/ProblemDetailsHelper.cs:155-173` — `Forbidden(reasonCode, detail, traceId)`.
  • `Services/Ai/Context/CallerSystemUserResolver.cs:36-45` — `ICallerSystemUserResolver.ResolveAsync(ClaimsPrincipal, ct)`: oid → systemuser, explicit Unresolved, never a guess. Already injected into `CreateEventAsync` (`EventEndpoints.cs:340`).
  • THE LIST REFERENCE IMPLEMENTATION (copy this shape): word-add-in-r1 task 062, `Api/Office/OfficeEndpoints.cs:1160-1183` (resolve the caller with ICallerSystemUserResolver; refuse with 403 when unresolved; never fall back). Its waiver: `tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.cs:646-659` (Permanent, "RESOLVED", query-is-the-gate); the communications waivers at `:612-640` are the same form.
  • `DataverseWebApiService.RetrieveMultipleImpersonatedAsync` (`:1030-1066`) — the impersonated read primitive. It has no $count; QueryEventsAsync needs one, so the impersonation goes through the existing `CreateAuthenticatedRequestAsync(..., impersonateSystemUserId)` parameter instead.
  • `tests/integration/auth/UnifiedAccessControl/DataverseWebApiServiceImpersonationTests.cs` — the existing way to prove what `DataverseWebApiService` SENDS (a hand-written recording handler through the service's protected test constructor; explicitly not `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`). Copy it to pin that the caller-scoped event query sends exactly one MSCRMCallerID with the caller's id and that the app-only one sends none.
  • `IGenericEntityService.GetEntitySetNameAsync(logicalName)` (`src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/IGenericEntityService.cs:67`; already injected into `CreateEventAsync` as `genericEntityService`; throws when the entity has no set) — the entity SET name from live metadata. Use it to turn a regarding type into the set used BOTH for the AppendTo check and for the @odata.bind, so the record authorized and the record bound are one value.
  • `Api/Filters/EntityAccessFilter.cs:115-157` (`EntitySetByType`) and `:174` (`TryResolveEntitySet`): has sprk_event → sprk_events but NOT analysis, account or budget, and carries a LOCKSTEP invariant with DocumentAssociationMap. Do not add entries to it.
  • `src/server/shared/Spaarke.Core/Auth/OperationAccessPolicy.cs`: bare record-scoped keys `"read"` (`:163`), `"write"` (`:242`), `"delete"` (`:247`) — "resource = the Dataverse record named by the route" (task 022 convention). `"finance.attach_invoice"` = AppendTo (`:193`) and `"finance.link_invoice"` = Write | Append (`:201`) are the precedents for "the record the lookup points AT needs AppendTo" and "the record that HOLDS the lookup needs Append". `"entity.associate_document"` = AppendTo (`:213`) names a document being filed and must not be reused for events. `HasRequiredRights` `:320`.
  • Tests: `tests/integration/contract/Api/Finance/FinanceEndpointsAuthorizationContractTests.cs` (compiled into the BFF unit project via `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests.csproj:77`) — the in-process host over the REAL `Map*Endpoints` (`:930-980`) and a CallerRecordAccessProbe subclass at its virtual seams (`RecordingPrivilegeProbe`, `:797`). `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Api/Events/EventEndpointsMembershipPublishingTests.cs` — runs the internal `CreateEventAsync` handler with boundary fakes (`:205-215`) and calls `BuildCreateEventPayload` directly (`:82`, `:94`; task 152). `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Workspace/TodoGenerationServiceTests.cs` (`:258`, `:264`, `:560`) and `TodoGenerationAssignedToTests.cs` set up `QueryEventsAsync` on a Moq mock. `tests/integration/Spe.Integration.Tests/EventEndpointsTests.cs` (983 lines) — route-shape expectations, including `UpdateEvent_HandlesInvalidStatusCode_WhenAuthenticated` (`:963-982`, expects NOT 404 for an invalid StatusCode on a random id). `tests/integration/auth/UnifiedAccessControl/OperationAccessPolicyCompletenessTests.cs` (discovers operation strings by source scan, `:46-102`, and lists known keys in InlineData at `:150-151`, `:241-242`, `:265-266`) and `OperationPolicyCharacterizationTests.cs` (`:101-102`, `:125-126`, `:156-157`).
  • `src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/IDataverseService.cs:14` — the composite IDataverseService INHERITS IEventDataverseService, so `DataverseServiceClientImpl` must implement any new member; its event members are fail-loud stubs (`DataverseServiceClientImpl.cs:2115-2185`, "RED-4 B").

TASK 167. Task 167 extends RouteAuthorizationGuardTests to govern every route file and adds a Pending waiver, owned by its fix task, for each of the 82 sweep findings. It has NOT landed on this branch (no 167 POML, and RouteAuthorizationGuardTests has no EventEndpoints entry). See constraint "waivers".</background>
