  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-003">Scope: all eight routes. Fail closed. A missing bearer token, a failed OBO exchange, an unresolvable caller, a RetrievePrincipalAccess or privilege-check fault, an entity-set lookup that throws, a record-type or name lookup that throws during the authorization decision, or any exception inside a check DENIES. There is no app-only fallback on any path. CallerRecordAccessProbe already collapses every "could not answer" into None or false; do not add a branch around it. The try around a check covers the decision only, never next() (the `RecordRouteAccessAuthorizationFilter.cs:191-205` rule).</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner round 9">Scope: the six /{id} routes. Denial shape. When the caller's rights on sprk_events({id}) do not include Read (this covers None and every fault), the response is the uniform 404: byte-identical, apart from correlationId/traceId, to the response for an id that does not exist and to the handler's own "event not found" 404 after the check passed. When the caller holds Read on the event but not the required right, the response is 403 with reasonCode `sdap.access.deny.insufficient_rights` (the caller can already see the record, so a 403 discloses nothing). No denial body contains the requested id. The handlers' existing 404 bodies (`EventEndpoints.cs:297-301`, `:510-514`, `:572-576`, `:900-904`, `:985-989`, `:1150-1154`), which today echo the id, are replaced by the uniform 404.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: the six /{id} routes. Required rights on sprk_events({id}), using existing bare keys: GET /{id} = "read"; GET /{id}/logs = "read" (Read on the event authorizes its log rows; the log query itself stays app-only, because sprk_eventlog rows are created by the BFF identity and an impersonated log query would return nothing for most callers); POST /{id}/complete = "write"; POST /{id}/cancel = "write"; PUT /{id} = "write", plus the new re-parent key (Write | Append on the event) when the body carries RegardingRecordType or RegardingRecordId, plus "delete" when the body sets StatusCode to `EventStatusCode.Deleted`; DELETE /{id} = "delete" (Delete, not Write: the act is a deletion, and requiring Write would let a caller who may not delete still delete).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: POST / and PUT /{id} regarding targets (the G5 pattern, owner round 3b / round 7 item 3). Check AS THE CALLER, then write AS THE APP. Create requires the caller's Create privilege on sprk_event via `CallerRecordAccessProbe.CallerHoldsPrivilegeAsync` (the privilege name read from live metadata in step 0, held in a constant beside `FinanceAuthorizationFilter.CreateInvoicePrivilege`, and pinned by a test); a missing privilege is 403 with reasonCode `sdap.access.deny.insufficient_privilege`. When a regarding record is given (on create, or as the NEW regarding on PUT), the caller must hold AppendTo on it, through the new regarding-target OperationAccessPolicy key. The regarding entity SET is resolved with `IGenericEntityService.GetEntitySetNameAsync(RegardingRecordType.GetEntityLogicalName(type))`, and the SAME set name is used in the @odata.bind, so the record authorized is the record bound. An unknown regarding id, a denied one, and a fault in the set lookup return the identical 403 (reasonCode `sdap.access.deny.insufficient_rights`). The event type (`EventTypeId`, sprk_eventtype_ref) is org-wide reference data and is not rights-checked; the Assigned To contact is server-derived (task 152) and is not caller-chosen.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: the order of checks on every route. (1) Pure request-shape validation with no I/O returns its existing 400 FIRST: Subject, Priority, RegardingRecordType range, StatusCode range, date order, and (new) on POST / and PUT /{id} "RegardingRecordType and RegardingRecordId are given together or not at all", and on GET / "regardingRecordId parses as a GUID". It discloses nothing about any record, so a validation error is never turned into a 404/403 and the existing validation tests keep their expectations. (2) Then the authorization filter(s). (3) Then any Dataverse read or write, including the handlers' existing app-only existence reads and the server-side name/record-type lookups. Checks that depend on the record's state (CanCompleteEvent / CanCancelEvent, `:1060-1085`) run AFTER the authorization check, because they would otherwise disclose state. On POST / and PUT /{id}, implement (1) as an endpoint filter registered BEFORE the authorization filter in the route's fluent chain, and move the handler's shape validation into it (one copy, same messages). Do NOT move the rights check into the handler: Rule A cannot see it there.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner round 9">Scope: GET /. The list is trimmed by running the event query IMPERSONATED as the caller (MSCRMCallerID = the caller's systemuserid from `ICallerSystemUserResolver.ResolveAsync`), so Dataverse applies ownership, role depth, BU, teams, sharing and hierarchy inside the query and TotalCount counts only trimmed rows. Add a NEW `IEventDataverseService` method that takes a REQUIRED `Guid callerSystemUserId` (not nullable) and passes it to the existing `CreateAuthenticatedRequestAsync(..., impersonateSystemUserId)`; `DataverseServiceClientImpl` gets a fail-loud stub for it in the RED-4 B style. Do not add an optional parameter to the existing `QueryEventsAsync`: the endpoint must not be able to reach the app-only query by omitting an argument, and `TodoGenerationService.cs:403`/`:570` keep calling the app-only method. Both methods build their URL with ONE internal static URL builder. An unresolved caller (not resolved, unparseable, or Guid.Empty) → 403 ProblemDetails with reasonCode `sdap.access.deny.caller_unresolved` and a correlationId extension, and no IEventDataverseService method is called (the `OfficeEndpoints.cs:1160-1183` shape). The existing owner narrowing (`_ownerid_value eq caller`) is KEPT, using the same resolved systemuserid; this task does not redefine which events are "mine". The handler stops calling `QuerySystemUserByAzureAdOidAsync`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner round 9">Scope: the list's OData filter (DataverseWebApiService.cs:330-331). `regardingRecordId` becomes a `Guid?` end to end (API query parameter parsed in the validation step → interface → URL builder), formatted with "D", so no caller text reaches `$filter`. A non-GUID value is a 400 before any query. No `$filter` clause in the shared URL builder is built from caller-supplied text; every clause is built from a typed value (Guid, int, DateTime).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-024 / #1098">Scope: the regarding READ shape, in the shared URL builder and MapToEventEntity. `$select` (list and get) never names `sprk_regardingrecordtype`; it selects `_sprk_regardingrecordtype_value`, `sprk_regardingrecordid`, `sprk_regardingrecordname` and the eight typed `_sprk_regarding{project|matter|invoice|analysis|account|contact|workassignment|budget}_value` columns. Filters: regardingRecordId given (with or without a type) → `sprk_regardingrecordid eq '{id:D}'`, and when the type is also given, additionally `_{thatTypesLookup}_value eq {id:D}`; regardingRecordType given WITHOUT an id → `_sprk_regardingrecordtype_value eq {refId:D}`, where refId is that type's sprk_recordtype_ref row, resolved in the BFF handler with `ICommunicationDataverseService.QueryRecordTypeRefAsync` (already injected into GetEventsAsync); when no row exists the handler returns an empty page with TotalCount 0 and a logged warning, and issues no query. MapToEventEntity derives the API's integer RegardingRecordType (0-7, unchanged contract) as the one of the eight typed lookups whose value equals `sprk_regardingrecordid`; when none matches, it is null. It never calls `GetInt32()` on a lookup. (The value-match rule is needed because a correctly written event regarding an invoice or analysis also carries a core-ancestor stamp in sprk_regardingmatter/project/workassignment.)</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-024 / FR-26 / #1098">Scope: the regarding WRITE shape, in BOTH the create payload (`BuildCreateEventPayload`) and a new internal static `BuildUpdateEventPayload` extracted beside it, so both are asserted without an HTTP test double. All values are resolved in the BFF handler and passed in the Dataverse request model as plain values (see "LAYERING"); the static builders only shape them. Write, in this order: (i) the target's own typed lookup as `{navigationProperty}@odata.bind = "/{entitySet}({id:D})"`; (ii) `{recordTypeNavigationProperty}@odata.bind = "/{recordTypeRefSet}({refId:D})"`, the row found by `QueryRecordTypeRefAsync(entityLogicalName)`, and the key left out (with a logged warning) when none exists, as TodoRegardingBuilder does; (iii) `sprk_regardingrecordid` = lowercase "D" GUID; `sprk_regardingrecordname` = the server-resolved primary name for matter/project (`RegardingRecordType.GetPrimaryNameField`, read only after the AppendTo check passed), otherwise the request's name; `sprk_regardingrecordurl` = `TodoRegardingBuilder.BuildRecordUrl(entityLogicalName, id)`; `sprk_regardingrecordnumber` (from `GetReferenceNumberField`) only if step 0 shows the column exists on sprk_event; (iv) the FR-26 core-ancestor stamps from `CoreAncestorResolver.DeriveForHostAsync("sprk_event", targetEntityLogicalName, targetId, ct)`, each emitted as `{stampNavigationProperty}@odata.bind = "/{coreSet}({stampId:D})"`, skipping the target's own lookup; an Unclassified outcome (account, contact, budget — `CoreAncestorResolver.cs:68-72`, a distinct non-error state) is a success with no stamp; an outcome that is not Succeeded (Status Error) refuses the write (nothing is written, and the route returns 500 ProblemDetails without the id). On a re-parent (PUT carrying a regarding), every OTHER `sprk_regarding*` lookup on sprk_event — the full live family recorded in step 0, i.e. the TaskActionCore list minus `sprk_regardingrecordtype`, minus the new target's lookup, minus the lookups just stamped in (iv) — is cleared in the same PATCH as `{navigationProperty}@odata.bind = null` (the documented Web API way to clear a single-valued navigation property; proven live in gate item (e), not during development). NEVER write `sprk_regardingrecordtype` as an integer and never write any `_x_value` key. Every navigation-property name, entity-set name and column name is read from live metadata in step 0, recorded in the task note, held as constants (the InvoiceReviewService `:284-300` precedent, e.g. a navigation-property helper beside `RegardingRecordType.GetLookupFieldName` in Models.cs) and pinned by a test. No logical name is used as a navigation property and no set name is made by appending "s".</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §11">Scope: new surface. Extend, do not fork. (a) Add overloads to `RecordRouteAccessAuthorizationFilterExtensions` (the method name must keep the `Add…AuthorizationFilter` shape so RouteAuthorizationGuardTests' `FilterMarker` (`:1898-1902`) credits it and the completeness scan's `FilterLiteralPattern` (`OperationAccessPolicyCompletenessTests.cs:46-48`) sees its operation literal): one for a FIXED entity set ("sprk_events") with a configurable route key ("id") and the /{id} denial shape above. (b) For the body-derived checks on POST / and PUT /{id} (regarding AppendTo, event Write | Append, Delete for StatusCode Deleted, Create privilege), a second overload on the same filter class that reads the already-bound request argument from `EndpointFilterInvocationContext.Arguments` (never re-reads the body stream) and asks `CallerRecordAccessProbe`. If that overload needs more than "(entity set, id, operation) checks plus one optional table privilege", STOP and report rather than copying FinanceAuthorizationFilter's declaration types. (c) The EXISTING overload `AddRecordRouteAccessAuthorizationFilter(string operation)` and its upload routes behave byte-identically: same route keys, same 403s, same short reasonCodes and detail text; its existing tests stay green unchanged. The new overloads use the `sdap.access.deny.*` reasonCodes named in these constraints and their own detail text. (d) Move `FinanceAuthorizationFilter.UniformRecordNotFound` and `RecordUnavailableReasonCode` into `ProblemDetailsHelper` with the bytes unchanged; leave same-named forwarding members on FinanceAuthorizationFilter so task 130's tests compile and pass unchanged; call the helper from the event filter and the event handlers. (e) Two new OperationAccessPolicy keys: `"event.attach_regarding"` = AppendTo (on a regarding target) and `"event.reparent"` = Write | Append (on the event being re-parented), each with a comment in the style of `:174-213`, each reached by a call site the completeness scan discovers, each added to the InlineData lists of OperationAccessPolicyCompletenessTests and OperationPolicyCharacterizationTests, and each with the three-question justification in the PR. (f) The new `IEventDataverseService` caller-scoped query method. Nothing else new: no new filter class, no new service, no new logical-name → entity-set map, no entry added to `EntityAccessFilter.EntitySetByType` or `SemanticSearchAuthorizationFilter.AuthorizableEntitySets`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: ExternalAccess zones. Do not modify any file under `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/**` or `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/**` (including CallerRecordAccessProbe.cs). Reuse them as they are. If a change there appears necessary, fire escalation trigger 5.</constraint>
    <constraint source="task 074 / owner round 9">Scope: waivers and the route guard. Add `new GovernedFile("Api/Events/EventEndpoints.cs", Scope.RouteLevelGate, "…reason…")` to `RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.GovernedFiles`, unless task 167 already added it. The seven non-list routes pass Rule A with a real filter and carry NO waiver. GET /api/v1/events carries ONE `new Waiver("GET /api/v1/events", WaiverKind.Permanent, "#1098", …)` whose reason starts "RESOLVED (task 159):" and states that the impersonated query is the boundary, that an unresolved caller is refused, and that TotalCount derives from the trimmed set (the `:646-659` form). If task 167 has landed on this task's branch: DELETE each of its Pending waivers for the seven non-list routes, and replace its Pending waiver for GET / with the Permanent one above (the task 127 precedent at `:612-640`). If task 167 has NOT landed: add no Pending waivers, and write in the PR description and the task note "167 not on branch; main session reconciles the eight /api/v1/events waivers at integration". The filters used must stay credited by `FilterMarker` and pass Rule B (`DecisionServices` `:1274-1296` includes CallerRecordAccessProbe). Do not change `ExpectedEndpointFileCount` (`:875`, 120) unless the endpoint file count actually changes (it should not).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-002">Scope: whole task. No Dataverse plugins. Every check and every write is in the BFF.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Scope: tests added or changed. No Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;, no DI-registration tests, no constructor null-check tests. Substitute at the CallerRecordAccessProbe virtual seams (the `RecordingPrivilegeProbe` pattern), `ICallerSystemUserResolver`, `IEventDataverseService`, `IGenericEntityService`, `ICommunicationDataverseService` and the CoreAncestorResolver's `IGenericEntityService` / `EntityColumnProbe` seams. Payload and URL shapes are asserted on internal static builders. What DataverseWebApiService SENDS is asserted with the hand-written recording handler in DataverseWebApiServiceImpersonationTests.cs. No live Dataverse in CI; live proof is the manual gate.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: every new guard. Prove it bites by seeding: remove it locally, confirm the named test FAILS, restore, and record each result (test name, what was removed, the failure message) in notes/task-159-events-authorization.md. Minimum seeds: each of the seven route filters (Rule A must fail naming the route, and that route's contract test must fail); the impersonation argument on the caller-scoped list query (the recording-handler test must fail); the 403 for an unresolved list caller; the GUID parse on regardingRecordId; the Delete check on PUT StatusCode Deleted; the re-parent Write | Append check; the AppendTo check on create; the Create-privilege check; the integer write of sprk_regardingrecordtype (the payload test must fail); the sibling-lookup clearing on update; the core-stamp refusal.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project hard gate">Scope: before the PR. Run the affected tests, the FULL BFF unit suite (tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests), NetArchTest (tests/Spaarke.ArchTests) and BOTH integration suites in full: `dotnet test tests/integration/Sprk.Bff.Api.IntegrationTests` and `dotnet test tests/integration/Spe.Integration.Tests` — not a build. Record pass/skip/fail counts in the task note. A filter that selects nothing reports 0 failures; prove each filtered run selected tests.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Scope: this task's PR. State the placement decision (in BFF: existing routes; no new service) citing `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`. Measure publish size against a FRESH build of origin/master and a fresh build of the branch, both from short paths, both zipped with Compress-Archive, with equal file counts; report both absolute sizes and the delta; ceiling 60 MB. Run `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive` — no new HIGH. Run `/conflict-check` before the PR (task 146 and the other sweep tasks share these files).</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner 2026-09-30 / round 4 (binding)">Scope: live Dataverse and Azure. Read-only metadata and record reads during development are allowed. Any live WRITE, the deployment, and the live gate are MANUAL steps for the main session, using existing non-admin test users in their current business units — do not relocate users, and do not use the root-BU users (Chelsea Friez, Lori Witkin, the hotmail guest) as the "denied" user. If no existing user fits a gate item, the main session asks the owner to create one.</constraint>
  </constraints>

