    <patterns>
      <pattern name="trimmed list by impersonated query" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Office/OfficeEndpoints.cs:1160-1183 + src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/DataverseWebApiService.cs:199-218">Resolve the caller with ICallerSystemUserResolver, refuse 403 when unresolved, run the query with MSCRMCallerID = that systemuserid (CreateAuthenticatedRequestAsync refuses Guid.Empty), no app-only fallback.</pattern>
      <pattern name="route-id caller-rights endpoint filter" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Filters/RecordRouteAccessAuthorizationFilter.cs:79-232">Route value → CallerRecordAccessProbe.GetCallerRightsAsync → OperationAccessPolicy.HasRequiredRights → fail closed; the try covers the decision only, never next().</pattern>
      <pattern name="uniform 404 for absent and denied" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Filters/FinanceAuthorizationFilter.cs:280-290">One reasonCode, no id in the body, used by the filter AND by the handler's not-found branch.</pattern>
      <pattern name="ADR-024 regarding set, Web API shape" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Finance/InvoiceReviewService.cs:284-300, :694-716 + src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Workspace/TodoRegardingBuilder.cs:131-280">Lookups only as @odata.bind with live-verified navigation-property names; the record type as a lookup to the per-environment sprk_recordtype_ref row; id/name/url denormalized; core stamp last, fail closed.</pattern>
      <pattern name="core-ancestor stamp on a hand-written JSON body" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Dataverse/CoreAncestorResolver.cs:452 (DeriveForHostAsync)">Derive the stamps without applying them; emit each in the payload's own shape; refuse the write when the outcome is not Succeeded.</pattern>
      <pattern name="in-process contract host over the real endpoint mapper" location="tests/integration/contract/Api/Finance/FinanceEndpointsAuthorizationContractTests.cs:797, :930-980">Minimal WebApplication, fake auth scheme, real Map*Endpoints, CallerRecordAccessProbe subclass at its virtual seams.</pattern>
      <pattern name="what DataverseWebApiService sends" location="tests/integration/auth/UnifiedAccessControl/DataverseWebApiServiceImpersonationTests.cs">Hand-written recording handler through the protected test constructor; assert headers and URL, not how they were built.</pattern>
    </patterns>
