  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Declare rigor FULL. Re-verify every anchor in the background against current source, and check whether tasks 146, 156 and 167 are on this task's branch. Then, READ-ONLY against live dev Dataverse, record in projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/task-159-events-authorization.md: (a) the attribute type of sprk_event.sprk_regardingrecordtype and its target; (b) the ReferencingEntityNavigationPropertyName of sprk_regardingrecordtype and of EVERY sprk_regarding* lookup on sprk_event (at least the 14 in TaskActionCore.cs:85-105); (c) the EntitySetName of each entity those lookups target and of sprk_recordtype_ref; (d) whether sprk_event has sprk_regardingrecordurl, sprk_regardingrecordnumber and sprk_regardingrecordtypelogicalname; (e) the live statuscode and statecode option values of sprk_event; (f) the exact name of the Create privilege on sprk_event; (g) whether `GET sprk_events?$select=sprk_regardingrecordtype&amp;$top=1` succeeds (it tells whether GET / and GET /{id} work live today); (h) one existing sprk_recordtype_ref row per API regarding type (0-7), or its absence. If (a) is not a lookup, fire escalation trigger 1 before writing code. If (e) differs from EventDto.cs:117-141, fire escalation trigger 2 and continue with the rest of the task.</step>
    <step order="1">Extend RecordRouteAccessAuthorizationFilter with the fixed-entity-set + route-key overload (the /{id} denial shape) and the body-declaration overload for POST and PUT, leaving the existing overload byte-identical. Move UniformRecordNotFound to ProblemDetailsHelper with forwarding members on FinanceAuthorizationFilter. Add the two OperationAccessPolicy keys and update OperationAccessPolicyCompletenessTests and OperationPolicyCharacterizationTests.</step>
    <step order="2">Wire EventEndpoints.cs: the validation filter ahead of the authorization filter on POST / and PUT /{id}; the authorization filter on the seven non-list routes with the rights in the constraints; the handlers' not-found branches return the uniform 404; correct the DELETE route's "Canceled" description (`:57-62`).</step>
    <step order="3">GET /: resolve the caller with ICallerSystemUserResolver (refuse 403 when unresolved), call the new caller-scoped query method, keep the owner narrowing, make regardingRecordId a Guid end to end, and repair the type filter, $select and mapping per the read-shape constraint. Add the fail-loud stub to DataverseServiceClientImpl.</step>
    <step order="4">Repair the regarding write shape in BuildCreateEventPayload and a new BuildUpdateEventPayload, with the live-verified names from step 0, the record-type lookup, the cleared sibling lookups on re-parent and the core-ancestor stamps from DeriveForHostAsync, resolving every value in the handler. Correct the "option set" comment at EventDto.cs:166-169.</step>
    <step order="5">RouteAuthorizationGuardTests: GovernedFiles entry and waivers per the waivers constraint. Perturbation-prove Rule A for each of the seven routes.</step>
    <step order="6">Tests for the closed set in the acceptance criteria; seed each guard; run the four suites in full per the hard gate; publish size and CVE per CLAUDE.md §10.</step>
