  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">GET /api/v1/events (finding: tenant-wide list, owner-filter bypass): through the REAL MapEventEndpoints host, a resolved caller's request reaches the new caller-scoped query method with exactly that caller's systemuserid, the owner narrowing carries the same id, and the app-only QueryEventsAsync is never called by the endpoint (asserted on the IEventDataverseService fake).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">GET /api/v1/events, impersonation is real: with the recording handler, the caller-scoped query sends exactly one MSCRMCallerID header equal to the caller's systemuserid and carries `$count=true`; the app-only QueryEventsAsync sends no MSCRMCallerID; the caller-scoped method with Guid.Empty throws before anything is sent.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">GET /api/v1/events, negative: when ICallerSystemUserResolver returns Unresolved (no oid, no matching systemuser, or a lookup fault), or a SystemUserId that is unparseable or Guid.Empty, the response is 403 with reasonCode `sdap.access.deny.caller_unresolved` and no IEventDataverseService method is called.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">GET /api/v1/events, injection (finding: DataverseWebApiService.cs:331): `regardingRecordId=x' or sprk_regardingrecordid ne 'zz` and any other non-GUID value return 400 and no IEventDataverseService method is called; a pure test of the shared URL builder shows a GUID regardingRecordId appears in `$filter` only as its "D" form, and every `$filter` clause is built from a typed value.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">GET /api/v1/events, read shape: the URL builder never filters or selects `sprk_regardingrecordtype` by its logical name; a regardingRecordId filter is `sprk_regardingrecordid eq '{id:D}'` (plus `_{lookup}_value eq {id:D}` when the type is given); a type-only filter is `_sprk_regardingrecordtype_value eq {refId:D}`, and a type with no sprk_recordtype_ref row returns 200 with an empty page and issues no query; MapToEventEntity maps RegardingRecordType (0-7) from the typed lookup whose value equals sprk_regardingrecordid, including for a row that also carries a core-ancestor stamp in another lookup, and maps a row with no matching typed lookup to null (pure tests on the builder and the mapper).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">GET /api/v1/events/{id} (finding: read any event; existence oracle): a caller whose rights on sprk_events({id}) lack Read gets the uniform 404 and IEventDataverseService.GetEventAsync is never called; a caller with Read gets 200 with the event as today.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">GET /api/v1/events/{id}/logs (finding: read any event's log): rights without Read → the uniform 404 and neither GetEventAsync nor QueryEventLogsAsync is called; Read → 200 with the logs as today.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">DELETE /api/v1/events/{id} (finding: soft-delete any event): rights without Read → the uniform 404; Read | Write without Delete → 403 `sdap.access.deny.insufficient_rights`; in both cases neither UpdateEventStatusAsync nor CreateEventLogAsync is called; Delete (with Read) → 204 as today.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">POST /api/v1/events/{id}/complete (finding: close any deadline): rights without Read → the uniform 404; Read without Write → 403; in both cases no status PATCH and no log row; Read | Write → 200 as today. An invalid status transition on a writable event still returns 400, and a caller without Read on an event in a non-completable status gets the uniform 404, never that 400.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">POST /api/v1/events/{id}/cancel (finding: cancel any event): the same four cases as complete, against the cancel handler.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">PUT /api/v1/events/{id} (finding: overwrite or re-parent any event): rights without Read → the uniform 404; Read without Write → 403; in both cases UpdateEventAsync is never called. With Read | Write: a body that carries RegardingRecordType and RegardingRecordId is refused 403 unless the caller holds Write | Append on the event AND AppendTo on the new regarding record; an unknown new regarding id and a denied one return byte-identical 403s; a body with StatusCode = EventStatusCode.Deleted is refused 403 unless the caller also holds Delete. A body with an invalid StatusCode on a random id still returns 400, and a body that carries only one of RegardingRecordType/RegardingRecordId returns 400 (validation before authorization).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">POST /api/v1/events (finding: attach an app-owned event to any record): a caller without the Create privilege on sprk_event gets 403 `sdap.access.deny.insufficient_privilege` and CreateEventAsync is never called; a caller with the privilege but without AppendTo on the body's regarding record gets 403 `sdap.access.deny.insufficient_rights` and nothing is written (no event, no log row); an unknown regarding id and a denied one return byte-identical 403s; the AppendTo check is asked of the entity set returned by IGenericEntityService.GetEntitySetNameAsync for that regarding type, and the payload binds the same set; a create with no regarding needs only the privilege; a fault in the entity-set lookup or the privilege check denies; a body with only one of RegardingRecordType/RegardingRecordId returns 400.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Uniform 404 (all six /{id} routes): the response for a non-existent id, for an id without Read, for a probe fault, and for the handler's "event not found" branch after the check passed are byte-identical apart from correlationId/traceId (status, title, detail, reasonCode `sdap.access.deny.record_unavailable`, extension keys), and none contains the requested id. Task 130's existing uniform-404 tests stay green, unchanged, after UniformRecordNotFound moves to ProblemDetailsHelper.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Fail closed (all seven filtered routes): with no bearer token forwarded, or with the probe throwing, the route denies (uniform 404 for the /{id} routes, 403 for POST /) and no IEventDataverseService method is called.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Filter reach: each of the seven filtered routes is exercised through the REAL MapEventEndpoints host; a test that invokes the filter class directly, or only asserts that a fake was called, does not satisfy this criterion.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The existing upload overload of RecordRouteAccessAuthorizationFilter is unchanged: its existing tests and the OBO upload contract tests pass with no expectation changes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Unauthenticated requests to all eight routes still return 401 (existing tests stay green).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Regarding write shape (#1098): pure tests on BuildCreateEventPayload and BuildUpdateEventPayload show, for each of the eight regarding types: no key `sprk_regardingrecordtype` holding a number and no `_x_value` key anywhere; the target's own typed lookup bound with the live-verified navigation-property name and set name pinned from step 0; `sprk_regardingrecordtype` bound as `/{recordTypeRefSet}({refId:D})` through its live navigation-property name when a record-type row exists, and absent (with a logged warning) when none does; `sprk_regardingrecordid` lowercase "D"; name and url present; each derived core stamp bound by its navigation-property name. On a re-parent, every other `sprk_regarding*` lookup in the step-0 family (not the target, not a just-stamped lookup, not sprk_regardingrecordtype) is set to null in the same payload. A test fails if any bound set name equals the logical name plus "s" where live metadata says otherwise (sprk_analysis at least).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Core stamp: a create or re-parent whose CoreAncestorResolver.DeriveForHostAsync outcome is not Succeeded writes nothing (no CreateEventAsync / UpdateEventAsync call, no log row) and returns 500 ProblemDetails without the id; a successful one carries the stamp in the payload (asserted through the CoreAncestorResolver's substituted IGenericEntityService / EntityColumnProbe seams).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">App-only background callers are unchanged: TodoGenerationService still calls the app-only QueryEventsAsync with no caller, and TodoGenerationServiceTests / TodoGenerationAssignedToTests pass (mock setups adjusted only for a changed parameter type).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">RouteAuthorizationGuardTests: Api/Events/EventEndpoints.cs is governed as RouteLevelGate; Rule A, Rule B and the census pass; the seven non-list routes carry no waiver; GET /api/v1/events carries exactly one Permanent waiver whose reason begins "RESOLVED (task 159):"; no Pending waiver for any /api/v1/events route remains if task 167 is on the branch, and if it is not, the task note and PR description say so. The task note records the Rule A perturbation result for each of the seven routes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No new logical-name → entity-set map exists; EntityAccessFilter.EntitySetByType and SemanticSearchAuthorizationFilter.AuthorizableEntitySets are unchanged (the diff adds no entry); no file under Api/ExternalAccess/** or Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/** is changed; OperationAccessPolicyCompletenessTests and OperationPolicyCharacterizationTests pass with the two new keys listed.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Every seeded removal listed in the "every new guard" constraint made its named test fail, and the task note records each one.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover exactly the behaviours listed in these criteria plus the fail-closed branches named in the constraints. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the task note.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF build green; the full BFF unit suite, NetArchTest, tests/integration/Sprk.Bff.Api.IntegrationTests and tests/integration/Spe.Integration.Tests all run in full and green (counts in the task note); every changed expectation in EventEndpointsTests.cs is listed in the note with its reason; publish size reported per CLAUDE.md §10 and at most 60 MB; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="false">MANUAL LIVE GATE (main session, dev, existing non-admin test users in their current BU, after deployment). Before running, confirm read-only (RetrievePrincipalAccess as each user) that user A has NO Read on event E and that user B has Read and Write on event E2 and AppendTo on matter M and project P. (a) GET /api/v1/events as A does not include E and its TotalCount does not count it; GET /{E}, GET /{E}/logs, PUT /{E}, DELETE /{E}, POST /{E}/complete and POST /{E}/cancel as A each return the same 404 body as GET /{random GUID}, and E's modifiedon and statuscode are unchanged and no new sprk_eventlog row exists for E; (b) B gets 200 on GET /{E2} and a successful complete (only if escalation trigger 2 is resolved or did not fire); (c) POST /api/v1/events by A regarding a matter A cannot append to returns 403 and no sprk_event row is created; (d) POST by B regarding M creates the event, and a read-back shows the matter lookup set, `_sprk_regardingrecordtype_value` equal to the matter's sprk_recordtype_ref row and the id/name/url columns filled; (e) PUT by B re-parenting that event to P: the read-back shows the project lookup set, the matter lookup cleared (null), and `_sprk_regardingrecordtype_value` on the project's row; (f) GET /api/v1/events?regardingRecordId=x%27%20or%20sprk_regardingrecordid%20ne%20%27zz returns 400. Results (ids redacted to their first 8 characters) recorded in notes/task-159-events-authorization.md.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>GitHub #1098 (existing). Sweep findings closed here (idor-group-159.json, all skeptic-confirmed), each named by an acceptance criterion: GET /api/v1/events (critical, plus the OData injection), GET /{id} (critical), DELETE /{id} (critical), POST / (high), PUT /{id} (critical), POST /{id}/complete (critical), POST /{id}/cancel (critical), GET /{id}/logs (high). Owner decisions applied: round 9 (fix pattern: reads as the caller, writes pre-checked as the caller then app-only, lists trimmed, fail closed with unknown = denied); round 3b G5 and round 7 item 3 (check as the user, create as the app); round 8 item 2 (the standard ADR-024 regarding set); round 4 item 1 (live-gate users). Related, not in this task: 146 (owner on create and re-parent), 156 (re-stamp the event's children on re-parent), 167 (route guard over every file), 132 (the 60-second None cache — not on this path, because CallerRecordAccessProbe is uncached). The same OData-injection shape may exist in other DataverseWebApiService query builders; the sweep did not verify that, and it is not in this task. Out of scope client-doc defects: the Copilot OpenAPI file documents regardingRecordType as "1=Matter, 2=Project" (the code is 0=Project, 1=Matter, 2=Invoice) and priority as 100000000.. (the API is 0-3). Reviewer amendments 2026-10-02 (adversarial review against the code): anchors re-verified on the work branch; "exactly one typed lookup" replaced with target lookup + FR-26 core stamps via DeriveForHostAsync (StampAsync writes SDK EntityReferences, not a Web API body); values resolved in the BFF because Spaarke.Dataverse cannot reach CoreAncestorResolver or ICommunicationDataverseService; MapToEventEntity derives the type by value match, not "which lookup is set"; the null-bind clear moved from step 0 (read-only) to live gate (e); the existing upload overload's short reasonCodes kept unchanged and the new overloads' sdap.access.deny.* codes named; the composite IDataverseService stub, the completeness-scan visibility of the new keys, the recording-handler impersonation test, the TodoGeneration mock setups and the ExternalAccess no-edit rule added; "changes the regarding" made "carries"; live-gate subjects chosen by Dataverse's own answer rather than by the parent matter (a lookup confers no access).</notes>

